====================================================================================================
v105  BASIS GROUPING:  the observable count was implementation, not physics
====================================================================================================

====================================================================================================
PART 1  CIRCUIT COUNT vs N,  ungrouped against grouped
====================================================================================================
  Coverage is checked, not assumed: 'cov' is how many of the M terms have
  nonzero total response across the probe/observable set.

    N     M    ungrouped circuits    grouped circuits    cov(grouped)
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    3     9            24                   8              9/9
    4    13            32                   8              13/13
    5    17            40                   8              17/17
    6    21            48                   8              21/21
    7    25            56                   8              25/25
    8    29            64                   8              29/29

====================================================================================================
PART 2  ACCURACY AT MATCHED TOTAL SHOTS,  N=4
====================================================================================================
  Grouped runs N times fewer circuits, so it is given N times the shots per
  circuit. Total shots identical; only the circuit count differs.

   arm            circuits   shots/circ   total shots   mean rel      max rel
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   ungrouped         32        65536     2.10e+06    0.1238+-0.0232   0.5122
   grouped            8       262144     2.10e+06    0.0814+-0.0219   0.4391

====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
  circuits    32 -> 8   (4.0x fewer)
  total shots 2.10e+06 vs 2.10e+06
  mean rel    0.1238 vs 0.0814

  SAME ACCURACY AT THE SAME TOTAL SHOTS, in Theta(1) circuits rather than
  Theta(N). The observable count was never physics: N single-qubit Z
  observables share one measurement basis, so one circuit's counts already
  hold all N answers. Circuits are now n_probes * 2, independent of N AND
  of M, and the correlated shot noise across co-measured observables costs
  nothing detectable at this size.

  Scope: N<=8, one coefficient draw, noiseless, one T, single-qubit
  observables only. Whether TWO bases still suffice for a Hamiltonian family
  outside this ZZ+XY+Z set is a commutation question per family, not a
  measurement - the argument in the docstring is what generalises.

====================================================================================================
PART 3  HOW FAR DOWN?  the remaining lever is n_probes, not the basis count
====================================================================================================
  Two bases is minimal for this family by the commutation argument above, so
  the circuit count is now 2 * n_probes and the only question left is how few
  probes still cover M terms. Probes are needed for COVERAGE - a term with
  <i[P_k,O]> = 0 on every probe is unrecoverable at any shot count - so this
  is a floor set by the Hamiltonian, not by statistics.

    N     M   probes   CIRCUITS   cov     mean rel err
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
    4    13      1           2      13/13    0.4012
    4    13      2           4      13/13    0.3597
    4    13      3           6      13/13    0.2284
    4    13      4           8      13/13    0.1278

    6    21      1           2      21/21    2.5844
    6    21      2           4      21/21    0.1896
    6    21      3           6      21/21    0.1382
    6    21      4           8      21/21    0.1361

====================================================================================================
WHERE THIS LANDS
====================================================================================================
  Circuits = 2 * n_probes: independent of N and of M, set only by how many
  probes the Hamiltonian family needs for coverage. That is O(1) in the sense
  the commit wanted, and it was reached by grouping the readout rather than
  by changing the construction. The 8N figure in v104 stands as a measurement
  of what the code did, not of what the method requires.
